Fuzz / Templates module (app/src/main/java/com/victorious/browser/fuzz/)

Curated starter wordlists — SecLists lineage
The bundled starter wordlists under app/src/main/assets/fuzz/wordlists/
(common-dirs.txt, common-files.txt, top-100-params.txt) are SMALL, hand-picked
subsets whose entries draw on well-known, widely-published web-content and
parameter name conventions as popularized by SecLists.
  - SecLists (https://github.com/danielmiessler/SecLists)
    License: MIT
The full SecLists is NOT bundled or downloaded by this app (honoring the
project's no-large-downloads rule); users import their own lists. This notice
credits the conceptual lineage of the curated starters and SecLists' MIT license.
No SecLists data files are copied verbatim into this repository.

Nuclei-style template engine — compatible subset only (no Nuclei code)
The template scanner is an independently-written, lightweight engine that
understands only a small subset of the Nuclei template shape (id, info,
requests[method/path/headers/body], matchers[status|word|regex|size]). It does
NOT claim compatibility with real Nuclei templates beyond this subset and bundles
no Nuclei (ProjectDiscovery) source or templates. The bundled example templates
under app/src/main/assets/fuzz/templates/ are original, safe exposed-file /
information-disclosure checks written for this project.
  - Nuclei (https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei) — MIT — referenced for
    the template-shape concept only; no code or templates vendored.

Minimal YAML parser
app/src/main/java/com/victorious/browser/fuzz/MiniYaml.kt is a hand-rolled
minimal indentation parser written for this project to avoid adding a YAML
dependency. No third-party YAML library is bundled.

