Fleet export + Metasploit RPC module
(app/src/main/java/com/victorious/browser/export/ and .../msf/)

Minimal MessagePack codec
app/src/main/java/com/victorious/browser/msf/MsgPack.kt is a hand-rolled,
first-party minimal MessagePack encoder/decoder (nil/bool/int/float/str/bin/
array/map) written for this project to drive the Metasploit msgrpc interface.
No third-party MessagePack library (e.g. org.msgpack:msgpack-core) is bundled
or depended on.

Metasploit RPC — interface referenced, no code vendored
The MSF RPC client targets the publicly documented Metasploit msgrpc interface
(msgpack over HTTP, /api/1.0/). No Metasploit (Rapid7) source is included.
  - Metasploit Framework (https://github.com/rapid7/metasploit-framework)
    License: BSD-3-Clause — referenced for the msgrpc wire interface only.

Fleet export — no third-party endpoints bundled
The export "fleet sink" posts a generic, secret-stripped JSON payload to a
USER-SUPPLIED endpoint. The HackerAI-Commander / Pentest-Swarm-AI API contracts
are NOT confirmed and NOT bundled; the target URL and auth are user-configured.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Batch G (feature/cert-evidence) — no new third-party dependencies.

The inspection-CA export/install helper and the recon evidence logger add no new
libraries. CA material reuses the existing Bouncy Castle dependency; evidence
ZIPs use the JDK's java.util.zip; screenshots use the Android framework Bitmap/
Canvas; report/index files use the already-bundled org.json. CA/evidence exports
to Downloads use the Android MediaStore framework API (no dependency).


-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Anti-Phish module (app/src/main/java/com/victorious/browser/antiphish/)

Defensive / educational only. No new third-party dependencies.
Punycode/IDN decoding uses the JDK's java.net.IDN. Homoglyph folding uses a
small first-party confusable map (inspired by Unicode TR39 concepts; no TR39
data tables vendored). Report JSON uses the already-bundled org.json.
Exports to Downloads reuse MediaStoreDownloads (Android MediaStore framework).
No credential capture, page cloning, or browser exploitation code is included.

